==English==

===Alternative spellings===
*[[inter-operability]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# The [[capability]] of a [[product]] or [[system]], whose [[interface]]s are fully disclosed, to [[interact]] and [[function]] with others without any access or implementation restrictions. For example:
#* {{military}} the [[ability]] of different [[force]]s to [[exchange]] [[service]]s so as to [[operate]] [[effectively]] [[together]]
#* {{computing}} the ability of [[software]] [[system]]s that may be running under different [[operating system]]s and [[hardware]] to exchange [[information]] through compliance with technical [interoperability] specifications, which typically define how different [[file]] [[format]]s and messaging [[protocol]]s can work together.

====Related terms====
*[[interoperable]]

